        "original_id": "02a9ca43-e24f-5833-a0f4-4ab0d782cc50",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Willow, Darwinia\n- Taxonomy: Salix, Myrtaceae\n- Topics: species counts, habitats, geographic distribution\n\nFacts:\n- Willow, also called sallow and osier, is the common name for the genus Salix.\n- The genus Salix includes around 400 species of deciduous trees and shrubs.\n- Salix species are found primarily on moist soils in cold and temperate regions of the Northern Hemisphere.\n- Darwinia, also commonly called mountain bells or bells, is a genus in the family Myrtaceae.\n- Darwinia includes about 70 species of evergreen shrubs.\n- Darwinia is endemic to southeastern and southwestern Australia.",
